**Deviations** (all recorded in the `src/render/graphviz/mod.rs` header)
1. **Oracle skeleton trimmed to keep c4**: the global `edge [ … ]` / `graph [ … ]` / `node [ … ]` default blocks and the `//` generated-by comment are omitted — the ge.dot_parser lexer rejects `//` and ingests the global attr blocks as spurious `edge`/`graph`/`node` NODE statements (observed during RED→GREEN), which would break the round trip. c4 (spec row) wins over oracle shape.
2. **Cluster labels**: emitted as `label=…` inside the cluster only when the group carries an explicit `label` attribute (c3's emission requirement, verified by p3). Name-fallback labels are NOT emitted: the dot_parser grammar has no graph-attribute statement inside a scope, so every named group would fail to re-parse ("expected a statement", observed). Tension between c3 and c4 is parser-side.
3. **Cluster ids**: named groups emit bare `subgraph cluster_<name>`, anonymous (empty-name) groups `cluster<N>` after group index — quoted subgraph names are rejected by the parser (observed); upstream quotes and renumbers `cluster0..N`.
4. **Arrows mirror the model** (c2 as briefed): `->`/`--` per edge direction; the oracle's always-`digraph`+`->` lossiness is not copied. Bidirectional edges append `dir=both`.
5. **Anonymous nodes** emit `#<node index>` (upstream uses odd global object ids; gently's model has no global object counter — the node index is the internal id).
6. Attribute mapping is minimal: `fill`→`fillcolor`, all else passthrough, values quoted per DOT identifier rules (`quote.rs`, unit-tested).

No new probes were run and no spec rows were amended; every contradiction above came from the shipped dot_parser contract, not from the pinned oracle.

**Next**
